 `tests/test_money.py`. The test expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring already described banker's rounding.\n\n## Change\n- `src/money.py`: switch the rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\n## Verification\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- Expected values: `2.675 -> 2.68` and `2.665 -> 2.66`.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main with alex requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even` (commit `08d3cd5986`), I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That is the only file touched.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit. The test's expected values (`2.675 \u2192 2.68`, `2.665 \u2192 2.66`) match half-even rounding.\n\nI did not merge anything. Merging into main still needs code-owner approval under the policy.", "type": "text"}]}]}